From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] venus: identify contexts in fatal command and object lookup logs

STEAMAC-G/A rejects incompatible image views and later loses a guest
context asynchronously. The final command-stream error and missing-object
lines identify neither context nor guest process. Nearby explorer.exe
teardown is not evidence that its context sent the invalid image view;
Xwayland/glamor may be a separate Vulkan client.

Append the renderer context ID and its debug name to dispatch diagnostics
(including the first fatal command and suppressed-bystander report) and
all failed object lookup variants. Preserve the existing diagnostic text
and fatal/lenient-destroy behavior. Decoders borrow the owning context's
immutable debug name, already alive until after the decoders are freed;
there is no extra allocation or log on a successful lookup.

Regression: host/virglrenderer/test/context-diagnostics.py uses the
renderer API and in-process server, no VM. Two contexts named Xwayland and
explorer.exe use the same missing command-buffer ID, and a third has an
invalid reply stream. Before: all five fatal/lookup lines lack identity
and the regression fails. After: all five identify their correct context.

Generated-by: LLM
